payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6d6891e73765cdc00797c9613fd4294d363195973f1c487ad372751fcacbd3fe","event_uuid":"a3c63ab1-eff1-490f-abaf-d56559e03ae9","position":{"commit_sha":"f7fa5e80514c0cd9f70b41aeba82d514a7947ae3","position":"1786808938916045001-a3c63ab1-eff1-490f-abaf-d56559e03ae9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aefcd381d6e54941959c4832073fcdd514ece16609fb8d1d6df79a17bca40e28","event_uuid":"dd77738b-2e9f-4f61-b627-e5b91d1de709","position":{"commit_sha":"43c53e5afa8162e79c1985478e22fe9d43d4d2e0","position":"1786809392434422001-dd77738b-2e9f-4f61-b627-e5b91d1de709"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"339f4ce8d8ed973b2cffe8e7cc4dfe0dfb09a129e926930314ffab5f0589de68","event_uuid":"4d622767-b85d-486e-8abd-3352a76a8a4b","position":{"commit_sha":"edc21be106a5ffe515695a7aaa4f53493777dd1b","position":"1786809804681457001-4d622767-b85d-486e-8abd-3352a76a8a4b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5a4c075e95bed8188c2ae58a4eeab7203b5045fd4649d79381f6df80c217c48d","event_uuid":"88cf3df8-6dda-4ef9-afaf-304cb35ae9a2","position":{"commit_sha":"f4748f54b6175ef45c64c1f52f145c6340790c92","position":"1786813396311995001-88cf3df8-6dda-4ef9-afaf-304cb35ae9a2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9e23637d77c85ade0181bcba6ec6f5ffd29fd4086f81bd6dcbca46f3736770c3","event_uuid":"a7745b9b-9d98-469a-b080-d835ab505705","position":{"commit_sha":"77d7cf24e2c4db084de5e9d87c353d6b8ac83bf4","position":"1786814470181132001-a7745b9b-9d98-469a-b080-d835ab505705"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786807640698988001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5c3b9e92-b373-4702-bd2c-6a2747691b24","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27"}],"description":"## Problem\nNothing validates, before a reconcile pass mutates a live client Jira, that the mapped\nprojects actually EXIST / are visible to the bridge bot. Two live-only failure modes:\n1. A mapped-but-nonexistent (or decommissioned / permission-lost) project key is\n   syntactically valid, so `_validate_project_key` passes; the failure only surfaces\n   deep in fan-out as an ACLI error. This is exactly the `05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27` incident class.\n2. `resolve_project` (projects_store.py) returns `mapping.legacy_default` VERBATIM,\n   unvalidated. Every unbound/legacy ticket (absent bridge_project) resolves there. The\n   cross-project write guard's allowed set = `read_projects().keys()` and EXCLUDES creates\n   (applier.py `_cross_project_targets`), so a legacy_default pointing at a real-but-wrong\n   (or nonexistent) project drives a mass CREATE storm into the wrong place, unguarded.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a reconcile-pass PREFLIGHT that runs BEFORE any outbound mutation and validates that\nevery project in `read_projects(repo_root).keys()` PLUS `legacy_default` (when set) is\nvisible to the configured backend. The probe reuses `access_check.py`'s existing\n`AcliClient` transport (the same Jira Cloud transport `run_access_check` already drives) and\nits retry helper (`_retry_sleep` / `JQL_RETRY_COUNT`). It enumerates the bot-visible project\nkeys through the client's ALREADY-PRESENT generic REST accessor\n`AcliClient._direct_rest_get` (acli_rest.py:207 — the same helper used by\n`get_issue_property`, `transition_issue`, and `validate_assignee_exists`) against the\nstandard Jira Cloud \"Get projects paginated\" endpoint `GET /rest/api/3/project/search`\n(paginated via `startAt` with the response envelope's `values[].key` / `isLast`). No new\ntransport class or subprocess is introduced — only a new `access_check.py` helper consuming\nthe existing `_direct_rest_get` accessor.\n\nBackend-neutrality: `access_check.py` is already Cloud/ACLI-specific, and this probe is a\nCloud-transport probe. The wiring GATES ON THE CONFIGURED BACKEND: it reads\n`rebar.config.load_config().reconciler.backend` and only builds the Cloud `AcliClient` and\nruns the probe when that key is `\"jira\"` (the Cloud/ACLI backend). For any other backend\n(e.g. `\"jira-datacenter\"`, whose pycontribs transport exposes no `_direct_rest_get` /\n`/rest/api/3` urllib path) the preflight logs an observable \"skipped: backend <key> has no\nvisible-projects probe\" message and returns without building a Cloud client or blocking the\npass. As defence in depth the helper itself also degrades (observable skip) if handed a\nclient lacking a callable `_direct_rest_get`. It only enforces on the Cloud/ACLI transport it\nis built for.\n\nOn a missing/invisible project (transport present, project absent from the visible set), FAIL\nFAST with a clear, actionable message naming the offending key(s) and the fix (correct\nprojects.json / legacy_default), rather than letting fan-out crash mid-pass. A hard\nauth/transport error (the probe cannot reach the backend) fails closed with its own distinct\n\"transport unavailable\" message, kept separate from \"project not visible\". Wire it at the\nreconcile pass entry (`__main__.py` `run_pass_result`, strictly before\n`reconcile.reconcile_once`), skipping read-only passes (dry-run / reconcile-check / preview).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A pass with a mapped key not visible to the bot aborts at preflight with a clear\n      message naming the offending key BEFORE any Jira write (no call to\n      `reconcile.reconcile_once`). Verified by\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q`.\n- [ ] `legacy_default` (when non-empty) is included in the preflight visibility check and an\n      invisible `legacy_default` is caught, naming it. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] An all-visible mapping passes preflight and the pass proceeds unchanged\n      (`reconcile.reconcile_once` is called; no happy-path behavior change). Verified by the\n      same test module.\n- [ ] A hard auth/transport error fails closed with its own distinct message\n      (transport-unavailable, not project-not-visible) and the preflight is observable via a\n      log/stderr message. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] A non-Cloud configured backend (`config.reconciler.backend != \"jira\"`, e.g.\n      `\"jira-datacenter\"`) is not blocked: the preflight logs an observable skip and the pass\n      proceeds without building a Cloud client. A helper handed a client lacking\n      `_direct_rest_get` likewise skips. Verified by the same test module.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q` —\n  fake/injected transport (no live Jira): a fake client whose `_direct_rest_get` returns a\n  `project/search` page listing `{GOOD}` visible, `BAD` absent → preflight raises naming\n  `BAD` and the pass makes no mutation; an all-visible mapping passes and the pass proceeds\n  (`reconcile.reconcile_once` called); `legacy_default=WRONG` (not visible) is caught; a\n  `_direct_rest_get` that raises fails closed with the transport-unavailable message; a fake\n  client lacking `_direct_rest_get` is skipped (pass proceeds). RED first: without the\n  preflight the pass proceeds to fan-out.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` from the worktree.\n\n## Sequencing\nLives in `access_check.py` (new mapped-projects preflight helper consuming the existing\n`_direct_rest_get` accessor) + wiring at the pass entrypoint (`__main__.py`\n`run_pass_result`). Disjoint from A/B/C/E files. Reads projects_store (no edit).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py","reason":"Add mapped-projects + legacy_default visibility preflight helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"Wire preflight at reconcile pass entry before any mutation"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py","reason":"New: fake transport, BAD absent -> abort naming key; legacy_default checked"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a011-491c-f7e5-4dd9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconciler preflight: verify every mapped project + legacy_default is visible in target Jira before any mutation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d0a25fd3-8105-4f3e-a585-a404ad5a76bd","c5d3bafb-8670-4d62-bfc1-ae13af47d9c8","5c3b9e92-b373-4702-bd2c-6a2747691b24","a3c63ab1-eff1-490f-abaf-d56559e03ae9","dd77738b-2e9f-4f61-b627-e5b91d1de709","4d622767-b85d-486e-8abd-3352a76a8a4b","88cf3df8-6dda-4ef9-afaf-304cb35ae9a2","a7745b9b-9d98-469a-b080-d835ab505705"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786814470181132002,"uuid":"261a961d-c5b7-43ad-897a-ee3e2b1a5b17"}